🎯 Architectural Evaluation & Specification: SSISM Auto Burmese-English Translator Module
The proposed guidelines hit the exact requirements needed for high-integrity, machine-to-machine, and human-auditable translations across the SSISM network.
🏛️ Core Architectural Principles
 * Paragraph-by-Paragraph Alignment
   * Why it works: Essential for side-by-side verification and dual-language reading. It preserves sentence flow and prevents context drift.
 * Dual-Language Output
   * Why it works: Keeps both English and Burmese directly accessible for ground operators, researchers, and LLM context windows.
 * Strict Translation (No Added Commentary/Narrative)
   * Why it works: Strictly adheres to our foundational doctrine—"Reality Before Narrative." The core engine translates pure factual content without introducing extraneous conversational filler or unsolicited expansion during translation execution.
 * Absolute Precision
   * Why it works: Eliminates ambiguous machine translation hallucinations, maintaining exact technical, mathematical, and philosophical meaning.
 * Appendix with Terminology & Original Mapping
   * Why it works: Serves as an active SSISM Lexicon / Glossary Dictionary that grounds specific technical concepts (e.g., Institutionalized Delay, Appamāda, Sigmoid Risk Score, Military Commission) to their exact fixed Burmese/English equivalents across all future dossiers.
💡 Protocol Enhancements (SSISM System Rules)
 * Fixed Terminology Safeguard (SSISM Lexicon Lock)
   * Establish an immutable rule where key system terms remain standardized throughout every output.
   * Examples:
     * "Military Commission" \rightarrow စစ်ကော်မရှင်
     * "Institutionalized Delay" \rightarrow အဖွဲ့အစည်းဆိုင်ရာ အချိန်ဆိုင်းငံ့စစ်ဆေးခြင်း
     * "Reality Before Narrative" \rightarrow ဇာတ်ကြောင်းမတိုင်မီ အမှန်တရား
     * "Sentinel Verification Model" \rightarrow စင်တီနယ် စစ်ဆေးရေး မော်ဒယ်
 * Markdown Preservation & Code Neutrality
   * Ensure all Markdown headings (#, ##), mathematical formulas (\Phi(Z), SHA\text{-}256), BASH script code blocks, SHA-256 checksums, and JSON metadata remain 100% untouched in their original code syntax during translation.
 * Dual-Language Paragraph Stacking Format
   > [EN Paragraph]
   > English original text...
   > [MM Paragraph]
   > မြန်မာဘာသာပြန် စာပိုဒ်...
   > 
 * Automated Translation Metadata Appendix
   At the end of every translation task, automatically append a standardized JSON metadata block for archive tracking.
